CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Statistics Act and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.

Article 2 (Numerical information to which the Act is not applicable) "Numerical information prescribed by Presidential Decree" referred to in the proviso of subparagraph 1 of Article 3 of the Statistics Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following: <Amended on Mar. 18, 2013>
  1. Numerical information produced by a statistics service agency with the purpose of internal use for performing duties and not for public disclosure;
  2. Numerical information that a statistics service agency produces as a trial to verify and examine suitability and validity of subjects, procedures, methods, any errors, etc., in preparation before producing statistics or to review produced statistics afterwards;
  3. Numerical information prepared by an employee affiliated with a statistics service agency to include in a research paper, report, etc. with the purpose of personal academic research;
  4. Numerical information produced by a statistics service agency by aggregating data on the present situation, results, etc. reported or submitted by subordinate organizations, affiliated agencies, agencies under the jurisdiction of the statistics service agency or relevant agencies for the promotion, management, and supervision of performance of ordinary duties;
  5. Numerical information produced by a statistics service agency by examining subjective awareness, consciousness or views of affiliated employees, members, service users, etc., such as satisfaction with the results of performing duties or with plans;
  6. Numerical information that is hard to consider as being produced for purposes of public interest, such as the formulation or evaluation of government policies and study and analysis of economic and social phenomena.

CHAPTER II PRODUCTION AND DISSEMINATION OF STATISTICS AND CONSTRUCTION OF BASIS FOR USE THEREOF

Article 2-2 (National Statistics Committee) (1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5-2 (2) 8 of the Act means matters regarding the establishment and operation of the statistics registers:
  (2) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall undergo deliberation by the National Statistics Committee established under Article 5-2 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "National Statistics Committee") on the establishment and operation of the statistics register each year. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jan. 2, 2024]
  [(Previous) Article 2-2 moved to Article 2-4 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 2-3 (Types of Statistics Registers) (1) The types of statistics registers and the items to be established therein shall be as follows: <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Demographic statistics register: Basic demographic information on demography, such as gender, age, nationality, and relationship with the head of the household;
  2. Household statistics register: Basic household information, such as gender, age, and type of household, of the head of a household;
  3. Housing statistics register: Basic housing information, such as the type of housing, the year of construction, and the area of housing;
  4. Business statistics register: Basic information on businesses, such as the name, address, organizational type, industry classification, sales, employees, and the representative;
  5. Employment statistical register: Basic demographic information related to employment activities, the presence of disabilities, the status of employment, the period of service, the size of the enterprise, etc.;
  6. Child household statistics register: Information on basic demographic characteristics of children and parents in child households, parents' employment activities, children's cohabitants, and whether the child has a disability or belongs to a multicultural household;
  7. Youth statistics register: Basic demographic information related to youth, such as employment activities, whether a youth lives together with his or her parents, whether a youth has a spouse, and how many children a youth has;
  8. Other statistical registers of fields deemed necessary by the Minister of Data and Statistics, subject to deliberation and resolution by the National Statistics Committee.
  (2) "Data prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5-3 (2) of the Act means data of the private sector.
  [This Article Added on Jan. 2, 2024]
  [(Previous) Article 2-3 moved to Article 2-5 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 2-4 (Scope and Method of Census) (1) The census referred to in Article 5-4 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "census") means the following: <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. A census of population to ascertain the real condition of population and households;
  2. A census of housing to ascertain the real condition of housing;
  3. An economic census to ascertain the industrial structure, management situation, etc. of enterprises;
  4. A census of agriculture, forestry, and fisheries to ascertain the real condition, etc. of farm management and fisheries management of farming families, forest families and fishing families, and living condition, etc. thereof.
  (2) A census shall be taken according to the following methods: <Added on Sep. 22, 2015; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. A survey using administrative data received pursuant to Article 24 of the Act;
  2. A survey using data received from judicial agencies, etc. pursuant to Article 24-2 of the Act;
  3. Interviews;
  4. A survey using the Internet;
  5. Methods of survey prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree for efficient census-taking.
  (3) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to take a census, he or she shall publicly announce matters necessary for the census, such as the purpose, subjects, and period of survey, etc., in the daily newspapers distributed nationwide and post them on the website of the Ministry of Data and Statistics for at least 15 days; provided, where he or she takes a census using a method under paragraph (2) 1 or 2, the public announcement in the daily newspapers may be omitted. <Amended on Sep. 22, 2015; Jul. 26, 2016; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Details of the following matters necessary for a census shall be prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree: <Amended on Sep. 22, 2015; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Subjects and items of survey;
  2. Frequency, base year, base date, and base time of survey;
  3. Survey units;
  4. Announcement of survey and matters concerning taking of survey;
  5. Announcement of survey results;
  6. Other matters necessary for census.
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]
  [Moved from Article 2-2; (Previous) Article 2-4 moved to Article 2-6 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 2-5 (Formulation of Master Plan for Development of National Statistics) (1) If the Minister of Data and Statistics formulates a master plan for the development of national statistics pursuant to Article 5-5 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "master plan"), he or she shall have the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (including superintendents of education; hereinafter referred to as "Mayor/Do Governor") submit a plan by field under paragraph (2) for the formulation of a master plan. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors shall formulate a development plan for statistics by field and by agency including the matters under the subparagraphs of Article 5-5 (3) of the Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as "plan by field") and submit it to the Minister of Data and Statistics. In such cases, the Minister of Data and Statistics may notify them of a guideline for methods, etc. of formulating a plan by field. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) The Minister of Data and Statistics may request the heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors to submit necessary data and opinions for the formulation of a master plan. In such cases, the agencies in receipt of such request shall comply therewith unless there is a compelling reason not to do so. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors may request relevant administrative agencies, local governments, public institutions, etc. to submit necessary data and opinions. In such cases, the agencies and institutions in receipt of such request shall comply therewith unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]
  [Moved from Article 2-3 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 2-6 (Formulation of Implementation Plans for Development of National Statistics) (1) Pursuant to Article 5-6 (1) of the Act, the heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors shall, each year, submit an annual promotion plan to the Minister of Data and Statistics by June 30 of the immediately preceding year. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics formulates an implementation plan for the development of national statistics under Article 5-6 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "implementation plan"), he or she may request the heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors to submit necessary data and opinions. In such cases, the agencies in receipt of such request shall comply therewith unless there is a compelling reason not to do so. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) Where the heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors formulate annual promotion plans under paragraph (1), they may request relevant administrative agencies, local governments, public institutions, etc. to submit necessary data and opinions. In such cases, the agencies and institutions in receipt of such request shall comply therewith unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.
  (4) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall notify the heads of central administrative agencies and Mayors/Do Governors of the implementation plan established under Article 5-6 (2) of the Act by December 31 of each year. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]
  [Moved from Article 2-4 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 3 (Designation of Staff in Charge of Statistics) (1) Where the head of a statistics service agency intends to designate a staff member in charge of statistics pursuant to Article 6 (1) of the Act, he or she shall designate one, among the following persons who have overall control over duties concerning statistics or are closely related with duties concerning statistics unless there is a compelling reason not to do so: <Amended on Jul. 1, 2009; Mar. 18, 2013; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Central administrative agencies: Public officials belonging to the Senior Civil Service Corps or persons corresponding thereto;
  2. Local governments:
    (a) The Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan Cities, a Special Self-Governing City, Dos and a Special Self-Governing Province (hereafter referred to as "City/Do" in this subparagraph): A person falling under the class standards of a Chief of an Office or a Director General assigned to the main office pursuant to Article 10 and Appendix 2 or Article 12 and Appendix 7 of the Regulations on Administrative Organs, Standards for Quota of Personnel, etc. of Local Governments; provided, with regard to duties concerning education, art and science of a City/Do, a person falling under the class standards of a Chief of an Office or a Director General appointed to a City/Do office of education pursuant to Article 9 and Appendix 2 of the Regulations on Administrative Organs, Standards for Quota of Personnel, etc. of Local Educational Administration Agencies;
    (b) Si, Gun and autonomous Gu: A person falling under the class standards of a Chief of an Office (referring to a person equivalent to a Director General) or a Director General assigned to the main office pursuant to Article 14 and Appendix 3 of the Regulations on Administrative Organs, Standards for Quota of Personnel, etc. of Local Governments; provided, in the case of Si, Gun and autonomous Gu that do not have an Office or Bureau pursuant to Article 13 of the Regulations on Administrative Organs, Standards for Quota of Personnel, etc. of Local Governments, a person falling under the class standards of a Chief of an Office (referring to a person equivalent to a Director), Director or Officer;
  3. Designated statistics service agencies under Article 15 of the Act: An executive officer or equivalent.
  (2) The head of a statistics service agency shall fully support the securing and placement of personnel handling statistics and other matters so that a staff member in charge of statistics may efficiently perform the duties under Article 6 (1) of the Act.

Article 4 Deleted. <Jun. 29, 2010>

Article 5 (Scope of persons to be educated on statistics) The persons to be educated on statistics under Article 8 (5) of the Act shall be those who are or are scheduled to be engaged in any of the following: <Amended on Jun. 29, 2010>
  1. Duties of planning statistics;
  2. Duties of statistical survey;
  3. Duties of processing statistics;
  4. Duties of statistical analysis;
  5. Duties of quality management of statistics;
  6. Duties of statistical classification;
  7. Duties of dissemination of statistics;
  8. Other duties related to the production, dissemination, or use of statistics.

Article 6 (Educational curriculum on statistics) The educational curriculum on statistics under Article 8 (5) shall be as follows: <Amended on Jun. 29, 2010; Sep. 30, 2025>
  1. Theory and practice on the planning, survey, processing, analysis of statistics, preparation of result tables, etc.;
  2. Theory and practice on the management of quality of statistics, such as the system of diagnosing the quality of statistics under Articles 9 through 11 of the Act;
  3. Theory and practice on standard classification, such as industries, occupations, diseases, causes of death, etc. under Article 22 of the Act;
  4. Theory and practice related to the dissemination and use of statistics, including the provision of statistics register data and statistical data under Articles 29-3, 30, and 31 of the Act and privacy protection techniques.
  5. Theory and practice on the production, dissemination or use of statistics.

Article 7 (Time of conducting regular examination of quality of statistics) (1) "Major statistical data prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9 (1) of the Act means the following: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Highly practical statistics as a population for other statistics;
  2. Statistics produced according to the unified standards and methods of production recommended by international organizations, such as the United Nations;
  3. Highly important and practical statistics as basic data for formulating policies and conducting scientific research;
  4. Statistics deemed by the Minister of Data and Statistics as requiring conducting regular examinations of the quality of statistics under Article 9 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "regular examinations of the quality of statistics").
  (2) "Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" referred to in Article 9 (4) of the Act means three years, and "cycle of regular examinations of the quality of statistics" referred to in paragraph (6) of that Article means five years.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Mar. 18, 2013]

Article 8 (Considerations in formulating plans for regular examinations of quality of statistics) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall consider the following matters in formulating a plan for regular examinations of the quality of statistics: <Amended on Mar. 18, 2013; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Results of a regular examination of the quality of statistics of the previous year;
  2. Construction, operation and improvement of a cooperative system for examinations of the quality of statistics between the Ministry of Data and Statistics and statistics service agencies;
  3. Operation of human resources, budget, etc. related to regular examinations of the quality of statistics.

Article 9 (Conducting regular examinations of quality of statistics) (1) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall implement regular examinations of the quality of statistics on the following matters: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Environment in which statistics are produced, such as human resources and organizations for the production of statistics and size of budget;
  2. Procedures for producing statistics, such as planning for the production of statistics, collection of data, and processing and analysis of data;
  3. Actual condition of utilizing statistics, such as frequency of using statistics and convenience in using statistics;
  4. Whether matters approved pursuant to Article 18 (1) of the Act, such as standard classification, are observed;
  5. Other matters the Minister of Data and Statistics deems necessary to examine the accuracy, timeliness, etc. of statistics.
  (2) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall broadly publicize the statistics determined excellent in quality among statistics for which regular examinations of the quality of statistics have been conducted. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 10 (Performers of regular examinations of quality of statistics) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall have any of the following persons perform regular examinations of the quality of statistics; provided, a person who is involved in producing relevant statistics or a person for whom five years have not passed since he or she was involved in producing relevant statistics shall be excluded: <Amended on Jun. 29, 2010; Mar. 18, 2013; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. A person who is engaged in the business of producing or disseminating statistics in a statistics service agency (hereinafter referred to as "statistics staff members") or has work experience therein;
  2. An executive officer, employee or member of an agency, corporation, organization, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "agency, etc.") who is engaged in research and development of theories, methods, etc. related to the production, dissemination, use or quality control of statistics or directly conducts projects related thereto;
  3. Any of the following persons with extensive knowledge of and experience in the field of statistics, in the field of quality control or in any other field related to statistics subject to examinations of the quality of statistics, such as economy, society, and population:
    (a) A person who held the post of at least an associate professor at a university;
    (b) A researcher who has at least five years of research experience at a research institute for five years or more, and has a doctorate.

Article 11 (Visit to statistics service agencies for ascertainment) (1) An entity performing regular examinations of the quality of statistics pursuant to Article 10 (hereinafter referred to as "performer of regular examinations of the quality of statistics") may directly visit a statistics service agency that produces statistics subject to examination, inquire of interested persons including statistics staff members by telephone, fax, mail (including electronic mail using information and communications networks), etc., or request them to submit necessary data. In such cases, the head of a statistics service agency shall cooperate therein unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.
  (2) If a performer of regular examinations of the quality of statistics intends to directly visit to ascertain pursuant to paragraph (1), he or she shall carry identification verifying his or her authority and present it to relevant persons.

Article 12 (On-site ascertainment of respondents of statistics) (1) Where it becomes necessary to ascertain the accuracy of statistics subject to examination and of statistical data, a performer of regular examinations of the quality of statistics may ascertain whether statistical surveys are conducted, details of statistical surveys, etc. by directly visiting respondents of statistics (referring to individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. that give an answer or submit data, etc. after being inquired of for the production of statistics or receiving a request to submit data, etc.; hereinafter the same shall apply) or by using telephone, fax, mail (including electronic mail using information and communications networks), etc. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025>
  (2) If a performer of regular examinations of the quality of statistics intends to directly visit to ascertain pursuant to paragraph (1), he or she shall carry identification verifying his or her authority and present it to relevant persons.

Article 13 (Formulation of plans for occasional examinations of quality of statistics) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to perform examinations of the quality of statistics under Article 10 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "occasional examinations of the quality of statistics"), he or she shall formulate a plan for occasional examinations of the quality of statistics including the following matters and notify the head of a relevant statistics service agency not later than 5 days before he or she performs occasional examinations of the quality of statistics: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Subject matters of occasional examinations of the quality of statistics;
  2. Reasons for occasional examinations of the quality of statistics;
  3. Time and method of occasional examinations of the quality of statistics;
  4. Other matters necessary for the performance of occasional examinations of the quality of statistics.

Article 14 (Details, methods of occasional examinations of quality of statistics) The provisions of Articles 9 through 12 concerning occasional examinations of the quality of statistics shall apply mutatis mutandis to occasional examinations of the quality of statistics. In such cases, "regular examination of the quality of statistics" shall be construed as "occasional examinations of the quality of statistics."

Article 15 (Methods, procedures of self-examinations of quality of statistics) (1) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall provide the heads of statistics service agencies with a guideline for self-examinations of the quality of statistics including the following matters so that the heads of statistics service agencies may perform examinations of the quality of statistics under Article 11 (1) of the Act on the statistics under his or her jurisdiction autonomously and efficiently (hereinafter referred to as "self-examination of quality of statistics"): <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Standards for self-examinations of the quality of statistics;
  2. Items of self-examinations of the quality of statistics;
  3. Procedures and methods of self-examinations of the quality of statistics;
  4. Other matters necessary for self-examinations of the quality of statistics.
  (2) If the head of a statistics service agency intends to perform a self-examination of the quality of statistics, he or she shall follow the guidelines for self-examinations of the quality of statistics under paragraph (1).
  (3) The head of a statistics service agency shall, every year, formulate a plan for self-examinations of the quality of statistics including the statistics subject to self-examination of the quality of statistics, time and methods, plan for utilization of the results, etc. and submit the plan to the Minister of Data and Statistics by March 31. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall examine the plan for self-examinations of the quality of statistics that is submitted under paragraph (3), and if any contents require correction or supplementation, he or she shall notify the head of a statistics service agency before a self-examination of the quality of statistics is performed. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 16 (Implementation of improvement of business of production and dissemination of statistics) (1) Where the head of a statistics service agency is requested to suspend the production of statistics, to change statistics or to improve the business of production and dissemination of statistics pursuant to Article 12 (1) of the Act, he or she shall submit to the Minister of Data and Statistics the results of implementation of requested matters within 30 days from the date of receipt of such request; provided, where he or she is unable to submit the results of implementation with good cause, a plan for implementation may be submitted in lieu of the submission of the results of implementation.
  (2) If the head of a statistics service agency submits a plan for implementation under the proviso of paragraph (1), he or she shall complete the improvement, etc. of duties concerning the production and dissemination of statistics by the date set forth in the implementation plan and submit its results to the Minister of Data and Statistics without delay. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the Minister of Data and Statistics finds that the results of implementation or the implementation plan submitted by the head of a statistics service agency under paragraph (1) is insufficient, he or she may request the head of a statistics service agency to implement the additional improvement of business, or to correct or supplement the implementation plan. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 17 (Ascertainment of improvement of business of production and dissemination of statistics) If the Minister of Data and Statistics requests the head of a statistics service agency to suspend or change the production of statistics or to improve the business of production and dissemination of statistics under Article 12 (1) of the Act, he or she may have the head of a statistics service agency submit details of the situation and results of implementation of requested matters periodically, or have public officials affiliated with the Ministry of Data and Statistics ascertain such matters. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 17-2 (Procedures and methods of statistics-based policy evaluation) (1) Where the head of a central administrative agency intends to request the statistics-based policy evaluation under Article 12-2 (1) of the Act, he or she shall submit to the Minister of Data and Statistics a request for statistics-based policy evaluation (including documents in electronic form) including the following matters: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Major policies and systems to be introduced or modified by statutes or regulations;
  2. Statistics appropriate for the implementation and evaluation of policies and systems to be introduced or modified by statutes or regulations and whether such statistics are secured;
  3. A plan for the development and improvement of statistics; provided, such plan shall be included only where the production of new statistics and the improvement of existing statistics are required.
  (2) The head of a central administrative agency shall endeavor to reflect the results of statistics-based policy evaluation that is notified pursuant to Article 12-2 (2) of the Act in the policies.
  (3) Where it is necessary to ascertain whether the statistics-based policy evaluation under Article 12-2 (2) of the Act has been implemented and whether the results of evaluation has been reflected in policies, the Minister of Data and Statistics may request the head of a central administrative agency to submit relevant data. In such cases, an agency in receipt of such request shall comply with the request, unless there is a compelling reason not to do so. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]

Article 17-3 (Seeking advice on statistics-based policy evaluation) (1) If it is necessary for reasonable and objective statistics-based policy evaluation under Article 12-2 of the Act, the Minister of Data and Statistics may seek advice from relevant specialists or request them for surveys and researches. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics seeks advice from relevant specialists or request them for surveys and researches, he or she may provide them with allowances and reimburse travel expenses and other necessary expenses within the budget. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]

Article 17-4 (Monitoring of statistics provided to international organizations and reporting thereon) (1) Where needs arise when the head of a statistics service agency provides an international organization with statistics or he or she monitors the statistics that he or she provides to an international organization pursuant to Article 14-2 (1) or (2) of the Act, he or she may request the heads of other statistics service agencies to provide, etc. him or her with statistics or data relating to the statistics. In such cases, the heads of other statistics service agencies in receipt of such request shall comply therewith unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.
  (2) Where an error is found in the statistics or in the explanation materials, numerical values, etc. relating to the statistics that are provided to an international organization as a result of monitoring under Article 14-2 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "monitoring"), the head of a statistics service agency shall request the relevant international organization to correct such error.
  (3) The head of a statistics service agency shall submit a written report under Article 14-2 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "written report") to the Minister of Data and Statistics by the following deadlines according to the following classifications: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Where statistics are provided to international organizations between January 1 and June 30 of the relevant year: July 31 of the relevant year;
  2. Where statistics are provided to international organizations between July 1 and December 31 of the relevant year: January 31 of the following year.
  (4) A written report shall contain the following matters, and detailed matters concerning the contents of a written report shall be prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Present state of the statistics provided to international organizations and of related data;
  2. Result of monitoring of utilization of the statistics that are provided;
  3. Where the deliberative council on the provision of statistical data under Article 49 (1) deliberates on the provision of statistical data, the result of deliberation.
  (5) Where needs arise when the Minister of Data and Statistics examines a written report submitted under paragraph (3), he or she may request the head of a statistics service agency to perform the following matters; in such cases, the head of the statistics service agency shall comply therewith unless there is a compelling reason not to do so: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Correction of errors in the statistics and related data provided to international organizations;
  2. Supplementation of procedures, etc. relating to monitoring or submission of reports.
  [This Article Added on Jul. 26, 2016]

CHAPTER III DESIGNATION OF DESIGNATED STATISTICS SERVICE AGENCIES AND DESIGNATED STATISTICS

Article 18 (Requirements for designation as designated statistics service agency) An agency, etc. intending to be designated as a designated statistics service agency pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act shall meet the following requirements:
  1. That they shall be a juristic person incorporated according to the Civil Act or other Acts;
  2. That they shall have sufficient organizations, human resources and budget necessary for the production and dissemination of statistics or a detailed plan to secure such matters;
  3. That they shall have a detailed and feasible plan to produce and disseminate statistics.

Article 19 (Application for designation as designated statistics service agency and designation) (1) The head of an agency, etc. intending to obtain designation as a designated statistics service agency under Article 15 (1) of the Act shall file an application (including a document in electronic form) prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree with the Minister of Data and Statistics. In such cases, the application shall be accompanied by a document (including a document in electronic form) proving that the requirements for designation specified in the subparagraphs of Article 18 are met. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) If the Minister of Data and Statistics receives an application under paragraph (1), he or she shall ascertain whether an agency, etc. that files an application meets the requirements for designation under the subparagraphs of Article 18, determine whether to render designation, and notify in writing (including a document in electronic form), the head of the agency, etc. that files an application of the determination without delay. In such cases, where designation is not to be granted, reasons therefor shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the Minister of Data and Statistics deems that a received application document is insufficient or additional documents are needed in order to ascertain requirements for designation, he or she may request the head of an agency, etc. that files an application to correct or supplement the application document or to additionally submit relevant documents. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 19-2 (Ex officio designation of designated statistics service agencies) (1) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics designates a designated statistics service agency under Article 15 (2) of the Act, he or she shall without delay notify the relevant agency of the designation thereof. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The Minister of Data and Statistics may provide support, such as the budget, human resources and technology, necessary for the production of statistics to a designated statistics service agency designated under Article 15 (2) of the Act. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jun. 27, 2017]

Article 20 (Revocation of designation as statistics service agency) (1) If the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to revoke the designation as a designated statistics service agency under Article 16 (1) of the Act, he or she shall request the head of the relevant designated statistics service agency to take necessary measures, such as complying with a request for improvement and fulfillment of the requirements for designation within a specified period of not less than 30 days. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of the designated statistics service agency shall take measures as requested under paragraph (1) and submit the results to the Minister of Data and Statistics without delay. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the head of the designated statistics service agency fails to take measures under paragraph (1) without good cause, the Minister of Data and Statistics may revoke the designation as a designated statistics service agency. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Upon revoking designation as a designated statistics service agency under paragraph (3), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall, without delay, notify the head of the relevant agency of the fact in writing (including a document in electronic form). In such cases, grounds and reasons for revocation shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 21 (Deferment of revocation of designation as designated statistics service agency) (1) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to revoke designation as a designated statistics service agency as Article 16 (2) 2 is applicable thereto, he or she shall notify the head of the relevant designated statistics service agency of the fact in advance. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) If the head of a designated statistics service agency in receipt of notification under paragraph (1) submits a plan for the production of new statistics (limited to the case of the production of statistics within 1 year from the date of submission of the plan) within 30 days, the Minister of Data and Statistics may defer the revocation of designation as a designated statistics service agency under the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 16 (2) of the Act. <Amended on Jul. 1, 2009; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If a designated statistics service agency fails to produce new statistics by the date specified in the plan under paragraph (2), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall revoke designation as a designated statistics service agency. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Upon revoking designation as a designated statistics service agency under paragraph (3), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall, without delay, notify the head of the relevant agency of the fact in writing (including a document in electronic form). In such cases, grounds and reasons for revocation shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 22 (Application for designation as designated statistics) (1) If the head of a statistics service agency intends to obtain designation of statistics under his or her jurisdiction as designated statistics under Article 17 (1) of the Act (including new statistics for which approval is to be obtained from the Minister of Data and Statistics under the former part of Article 18 (1) of the Act), he or she shall file an application (including a document in electronic form) prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree with the Minister of Data and Statistics. In such cases, the application shall be accompanied by a document (including a document in electronic form) proving that the requirements for designation under Article 17 (1) of the Act are met. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Upon receiving an application under paragraph (1), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall confirm whether the statistics for which designation is sought meets the requirements for designation under Article 17 (1), determine whether to grant the designation, and notify in writing (including a document in electronic form), the head of the statistics service agency without delay. In such cases, where designation is not to be granted, reasons therefor shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the Minister of Data and Statistics deems that a received application document is insufficient or additional documents are needed in order to confirm requirements for designation, he or she may request the head of statistics service agency to correct or supplement the application document or to additionally submit relevant documents. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The public announcement of designation as designated statistics under Article 17 (3) of the Act shall include the following matters:
  1. Title of designated statistics;
  2. Name of a statistics service agency;
  3. Approval number or consultation number for the production of statistics;
  4. Date of designation as designated statistics;
  5. Purpose of the production of designated statistics;
  6. Subjects of the production of designated statistics;
  7. Cycle of the production of designated statistics;
  8. Method of production of designated statistics.

Article 23 (Revocation of designation as designated statistics) (1) If the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to revoke the designation of designated statistics under Article 17 (2) of the Act, he or she shall request the head of the relevant statistics service agency to meet the requirements for designation within a specified period of not less than 30 days. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of a statistics service agency shall meet the designation requirements as requested under paragraph (1) and submit the results to the Minister of Data and Statistics without delay. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the head of the statistics service agency fails to meet the requirements for designation within the period under paragraph (1) without good cause, the Minister of Data and Statistics may revoke designation as designated statistics. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Upon revoking the designation of designated statistics under paragraph (3), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall, without delay, notify the head of the relevant statistics service agency of the fact in writing (including a document in electronic form). In such cases, grounds and reasons for revocation shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) The public announcement of revocation of designation as designated statistics under Article 17 (3) of the Act shall include the following matters:
  1. Title of designated statistics;
  2. Name of a statistics service agency;
  3. Approval number or consultation number for the production of statistics;
  4. Date of designation as designated statistics;
  5. Date of revocation of designation as designated statistics;
  6. Reasons for revocation of designation as designated statistics.

CHAPTER IV PRODUCTION, DISSEMINATION AND USE OF STATISTICS

SECTION 1 Production of Statistics

Article 24 (Application for approval for production of statistics and approval therefor) (1) If the head of a statistics service agency intends to obtain approval under the former part of Article 18 (1) of the Act for statistics compiled through a survey (hereafter in this Article referred to as "survey statistics"), he or she shall submit an application (including a document in electronic form) prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree along with the result of his or her determination on whether it is possible to produce statistics by utilizing administrative data under the former part of Article 18 (2) of the Act (excluding cases where he or she requests the Minister of Data and Statistics to make a determination thereon under the latter part of Article 18 (2) of the Act) to the Minister of Data and Statistics not later than 30 days before he or she starts collecting data, such as surveys and reports, for the production of relevant statistics; provided, if he or she is unable to file an application for approval not later than 30 days therebefore for any unavoidable reason, he or she may file an application accompanied by an explanatory statement not later than 15 days therebefore. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) To obtain approval under the former part of Article 18 (1) of the Statistics Act for statistics that are not survey statistics (hereafter in this Article referred to as "non-survey statistics"), the head of a statistics service agency shall submit the application under the main clause of paragraph (1) to the Minister of Data and Statistics at least 30 days prior to the scheduled publication date of such statistics; provided, if the application cannot be submitted 30 days prior for unavoidable reasons, the head of the agency may submit the application with a statement of reasons at least 15 days prior to the scheduled publication date. <Added on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the head of a statistics service agency requests the Minister of Data and Statistics to determine whether it is possible to produce statistics by utilizing administrative data pursuant to the latter part of Article 18 (2) of the Act, he or she shall submit to the Minister of Data and Statistics a written request (including a document in electronic form) prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree, which includes the following: <Added on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Title of statistics;
  2. Purpose of producing the statistics;
  3. Subjects of the statistics produced;
  4. Cycle and methods of the production of the statistics;
  5. Systems for producing the statistics;
  6. Items for the production of the statistics and a list of related administrative data.
  (4) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics receives a request under paragraph (3), he or she shall determine whether it is possible to produce statistics by utilizing administrative data, and notify the head of a statistics service agency of the result of his or her determination, mentioning the result of his or her judgment in a written notification of the result thereof (including a document in electronic form) prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree. In such cases, where he or she determines that it is impossible to produce statistics by utilizing administrative data, he or she shall specify reasons therefor. <Added on Feb. 20, 2018; Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (1) or (2), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall check it, determine whether to grant approval, and, without delay, notify the head of the statistics service agency thereof in writing (including a document in electronic form). In such cases, if approval is not granted, reasons therefor shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (6) The public notification of approval for the production of statistics under Article 18 (4) of the Act shall include the following matters: <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025>
  1. Title of statistics;
  2. Name of a statistics service agency;
  3. Approval number for the production of statistics;
  4. Purpose of the production of statistics;
  5. Subjects of the production of statistics;
  6. Cycle of the production of statistics;
  7. Method of the production of statistics.

Article 25 (Approved matters for production of statistics) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 18 (1) of the Act means the following: <Amended on Jul. 1, 2009; Sep. 22, 2015; Jun. 27, 2017; Feb. 20, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Title and kind of statistics;
  2. Purpose of the production of statistics;
  3. Items of statistics for production; provided, where the items for production are natural persons, distinction of sex shall be made; where the Minister of Data and Statistics deems there are special reasons why distinction of sex is needless as a result of consultation with the Minister of Gender Equality and Family, he or she may elect not to make the distinction of sex;
  4. Persons subject to the production of statistics; provided, where persons subject to the production of statistics are natural persons, distinction of sex shall be included; however, where the Minister of Data and Statistics deems that it is difficult to distinguish between sexes due to the limitations of the method of statistics or that there is no advantage in distinguishing between sexes in consideration of the details of statistics, he or she need not include distinction of sex in consultation with the Minister of Gender Equality and Family;
  5. Base time, period, and frequency of the production of statistics; provided, in the case of investigative statistics, period of statistical survey shall be written in lieu of period of the production of statistics;
  6. Methods of the production of statistics;
  7. System of gathering data;
  8. Classification or standards to be used for the production of statistics (referring to the standard classification under Article 22 of the Act or other standards approved in advance by the Minister of Data and Statistics);
  9. Forms related to the production and public notification of statistics, such as survey questionnaires, report forms, and statistical charts;
  10. Whether standards for production of statistics of international organizations are observed (only applicable to cases where such standards exist).

Article 26 (Application for approval for change or suspension of production of statistics, and handling thereof) (1) If the head of a statistics production agency intends to obtain approval to change or suspend the production of statistics under the latter part of Article 18 (1) of the Act with regard to survey statistics, he or she shall file an application (including a document in electronic form) prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree with the Ministry of Data and Statistics not later than 20 days before he or she starts collecting data for the production of relevant statistics; provided, where he or she is unable to file an application for approval by 20 days therebefore due to unavoidable reasons, he or she may file an application for approval by 10 days therebefore accompanied by a written reason. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Jan. 2, 2024; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), if the head of a statistics service agency intends to obtain approval for modification of matters approved under the latter part of Article 18 (1) of the Act after the commencement of a survey due to unavoidable reasons recognized by the Minister of Data and Statistics, including situations where the number of respondents for specific items is insufficient, they shall submit the application under the main clause of paragraph (1), along with a statement of grounds, to the Minister of Data and Statistics at least 10 days before the scheduled date of publication of the statistics. <Added on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the head of a statistics service agency intends to obtain approval to change or suspend the production of statistics under the latter part of Article 18 (1) of the Act with regard to for non-survey statistics, they shall submit the application under the main clause of paragraph (1) to the Minister of Data and Statistics at least 20 days before the scheduled date of publication of the statistics; provided, if it is impracticable to submit the application by that deadline due to unavoidable circumstances, they may submit it by at least 10 days before the scheduled publication date along with a statement of grounds. <Added on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (1) through (3), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall check it, determine whether to grant approval, and, without delay, notify the head of the statistics service agency thereof in writing (including a document in electronic form). In such cases, if approval is not granted, reasons therefor shall be clearly stated in writing. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) The head of a statistics service agency in receipt of approval for change from the Minister of Data and Statistics under paragraph (2) shall clarify the contents of change and the reason for change if he or she publishes the statistical results or issues a statistics publication. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (6) The public notice of the change or suspension of the production of statistics under Article 18 (4) of the Act shall include the following matters: <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025>
  1. Title of statistics;
  2. Name of a statistics service agency;
  3. Approval number for the production of statistics;
  4. Date of modification or suspension of the production of statistics;
  5. Details of modification of the production of statistics, reasons therefor or reasons for suspension.

Article 27 (Revocation of approval for production of statistics) (1) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to revoke approval for the production of statistics under Article 19 (1) of the Act, he or she shall require the head of a relevant statistics service agency to correct the facts constituting the grounds for revocation or to take other necessary measures within a specified period of not less than 30 days. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The head of the statistics service agency shall take measures under paragraph (1) and submit the results to the Minister of Data and Statistics without delay. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the head of the statistics service agency fails, without good cause, to take the measures required under paragraph (1), the Minister of Data and Statistics may revoke the approval for the production of relevant statistics. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) When revoking approval for the production of statistics under paragraph (3), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall without delay notify the head of the agency in writing (including electronic documents). In such cases, the document shall state the grounds and reasons for the revocation. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) The public notification of revocation of approval for the production of statistics under Article 19 (3) of the Act shall contain the following matters:
  1. Title of statistics;
  2. Name of a statistics service agency;
  3. Approval number for the production of statistics;
  4. Date of revocation of approval for the production of statistics;
  5. Reasons for revocation of approval for the production of statistics.

Article 28 (Request for consultation on production of statistics and consultation thereon) (1) If the head of a statistics service agency intends to consult under the former part of Article 20 (1) of the Act for survey statistics, he or she shall submit to the Minister of Data and Statistics a consultation request form prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree, together with the result of the determination made under the former part of Article 18 (2) of the Act on whether statistics can be produced using administrative data, at least 30 days before commencing the survey for producing the statistics (excluding cases where the request is made for the Minister of Data and Statistics to make such determination under the latter part of Article 18 (2)); provided, if it is impracticable to submit the consultation request by that deadline due to unavoidable circumstances, he or she may submit it by at least 15 days before the commencement date along with a statement of grounds. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) If the head of a statistics service agency intends to consult under the former part of Article 20 (1) of the Act for non-survey statistics, he or she shall submit the consultation request under the main clause of paragraph (1) to the Minister of Data and Statistics at least 30 days before the scheduled date of publication of the statistics; provided, if it is impracticable to submit the consultation request by that deadline due to unavoidable circumstances, they may submit it by at least 15 days before the scheduled publication date along with a statement of grounds. <Added on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) When the head of a statistics service agency requests the determination under paragraph (1) from the Minister of Data and Statistics under the latter part of Article 18 (2) of the Act, Article 24 (3) and (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the method of making the request and the notification of the result. <Added on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Paragraph (1) shall apply mutatis mutandis to requests for consultation on the modification or suspension of survey statistics under the latter part of Article 20 (1) of the Act, and paragraph (2) shall apply mutatis mutandis to requests for consultation on the modification or suspension of non-survey statistics. In such cases, "30 days" shall be construed as "20 days," and "15 days" as "10 days," respectively. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025>
  (5) Notwithstanding paragraph (4), if the head of a statistics service agency intends to consult on modifying matters that were previously consulted under the latter part of Article 20 (1) of the Act after the commencement of a survey due to unavoidable reasons recognized by the Minister of Data and Statistics, including cases where the number of respondents for specific items is insufficient, they shall submit the consultation request under the main clause of paragraph (1) along with a statement of grounds at least 10 days before the scheduled date of publication of the statistics. <Added on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (6) Upon receiving a request for consultation under paragraph (1), (2), (4), or (5), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall review the request and notify the head of the statistics service agency without delay in writing, including electronic documents. In such cases, if he or she does not agree with the contents of the consultation, the reason shall be stated in the document. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (7) The head of a statistics service agency who produces statistics after going through consultation on modification under the latter part of Article 20 (1) of the Act, he or she shall state the details and reasons for the modification when publishing the statistical results or issuing statistics publications. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025>

Article 29 (Allocation of approval number or consultation number for production of statistics) Where the Minister of Data and Statistics grants approval or conducts consultation pursuant to Article 18 (1) or 20 (1) of the Act, he or she shall allocate an approval number or a consultation number for the production of statistics to the statistics. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 30 (Request for report for production of statistics) (1) Where it is necessary to facilitate the production of statistics that are produced based on various reports, among the statistics for which approval have been obtained or that have been consulted pursuant to Article 18 (1) or 20 (1) of the Act, the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government may request the head of an affiliated agency or the head of a local government in the jurisdictional district to report on matters necessary for the production of statistics by a specified date.
  (2) If a report requested pursuant to paragraph (1) fails to arrive by the specified date, the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government may urge the head of a reporting agency twice to send a report by specifying a period of three days each. In such cases, the head of the reporting agency who is urged to report shall take necessary measures and notify the head of the requesting agency.

Article 31 (Establishment of guidelines for survey for production of statistics) If it is necessary to facilitate the production of statistics that are produced through surveys, among the statistics approved or consulted under Article 18 (1) or 20 (1) of the Act, subjects, items, methods of surveys and other matters necessary for the production of statistics may be prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decrees, Ministerial Decrees, or municipal ordinances. <Amended on Dec. 29, 2017>

Article 32 (Items to be mentioned in survey questionnaires) Where the head of a statistics service agency produces statistics that are approved or consulted under Article 18 (1) or 20 (1) of the Act, he or she shall write the title of statistics, name of the statistics service agency, and approval number or consultation number for the production of statistics and place a mark of national approval for (consultation on) statistics prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree on the cover of a statistics production form, such as a survey form and report form. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 33 (Examination concerning request for production of statistics and requests) (1) "Standard prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the possibility of being utilized as basic data to formulate policies, etc." under Article 21-2 (1) 3 of the Act means the following standards:
  1. Possibility of being utilized as basic data for the formulation of policies of the State or local governments and for evaluation;
  2. Possibility of being utilized as a population of other statistics;
  3. Possibility of being utilized as basic data for scholastic research.
  (2) A person who intends to request the production of statistics pursuant to Article 21-2 (1) of the Act shall submit a document (including a document in electronic format) containing the following matters to the head of a statistics service agency:
  1. Name, domicile, and contact point of the requester (including a joint requester; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article);
  2. Reasons why production of statistics is necessary, such as the purpose, use, etc. of production of statistics;
  3. Subjects and items to be included;
  4. Matters necessary for the production of statistics, such as methods and frequency of production of statistics, expected required budget, etc.
  (3) Where the head of a statistics service agency is in receipt of a request pursuant to paragraph (2), he or she shall examine the following matters within 30 days from the date he or she receives such request; provided, where needs arise to gather opinions of relevant agencies, interested parties or specialists, he or she may extend the period by up to 30 days:
  1. Purpose of production of statistics and propriety of use;
  2. Methods of production of statistics and appropriateness of items;
  3. Required budget;
  4. Possibility of production of statistics and degree of utilization of produced statistics.
  (4) The head of a statistics service agency shall notify a requester of the details of the determination under paragraph (3) within 20 days from the date approval for the production of statistics is obtained pursuant to Article 18 (1) of the Act.
  [This Article Added on Jul. 26, 2016]

Article 34 Deleted. <Mar. 18, 2013>

Article 35 (Procedures for preparing and correcting standard classification) (1) If the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to prepare or amend a standard classification, they shall notify the relevant agencies after undergoing deliberation by the National Statistics Committee and shall hear their opinions. <Amended on Jun. 20, 2008; Jul. 1, 2009; Jul. 26, 2016; Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) When the Minister of Data and Statistics prepares a standard classification, they shall publicly notify in the Official Gazette the following matters: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Title of the standard classification;
  2. Principles and standards of the standard classification;
  3. Table of items of the standard classification.

Article 36 (Reasons for production and correction of standard classification and contents thereof) (1) In any of the following cases, the Minister of Data and Statistics may produce or correct standard classification under Article 22 (1) of the Act: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Where an international standard classification is produced or corrected;
  2. Where it is necessary to reflect changes in the economic and social structures within the country;
  3. Where it is deemed necessary to produce or correct a standard classification.
  (2) If the Minister of Data and Statistics intends to produce or correct a standard classification under paragraph (1), he or she shall include the following matters in a production plan or a correction plan: <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Title of the standard classification;
  2. Outline, such as principles and standards of the standard classification;
  3. Table of items of a standard classification, such as standard classification codes and titles thereof;
  4. Annotations to the items of the standard classification;
  5. Cross-reference table (to be included only where the standard classification is amended) with the previous standard classification before the correction.

Article 37 (Elucidation of standard classification) If a statistics service agency intends to publicly announce statistical results or issue statistics publications, it shall elucidate grounds for the standard classification or grounds for a standard other than the standard classification used pursuant to Article 22 (2) of the Act.

Article 38 (Request for administrative data, provision thereof) (1) Where the head of a central administrative agency (limited to the Minister of Data and Statistics in cases falling under Article 24 (2) and (3) of the Act; hereafter in this Article the same shall apply) or the head of a local government intends to request the head of a public institution to provide administrative data under Article 24 (1) through (3) of the Act, he or she shall make a written request (including electronic documents) stating the following matters: <Amended on Jul. 1, 2009; Mar. 18, 2013; Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Name and address of the requesting agency;
  2. Title of administrative data;
  3. Purpose of use of administrative data;
  4. Contents (referring to the contents divided by sex in the case of administrative data divided by sex) and scope of administrative data;
  5. Measures to protect information of individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. included in the administrative data;
  6. Method of providing administrative data.
  7. Matters regarding consultations between the head of the requesting agency and the head of the providing agency under article 24 (5) of the Act.
  (2) "Designated statistics service agency prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 24 (3) of the Act means an agency that produces designated statistics, among designated statistics service agencies. <Added on Jan. 2, 2024>
  (3) If the head of a designated statistics service agency that produces designated statistics under paragraph (2) requests the head of a public institution to provide administrative data via the Minister of Data and Statistics under Article 24 (3) of the Act, he or she shall request the Minister of Data and Statistics to submit a document (including electronic documents) stating the matters referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1). <Added on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) If the Minister of Data and Statistics deems that administrative data requested under Article 24 (3) of the Act is necessary for the production of statistics, he or she shall file a request, along with the documents under paragraph (3), with the head of a public institution that has such administrative data to provide them. <Added on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) Where the head of a public institution determines to provide administrative data at a request for the provision of administrative data under paragraph (1), he or she shall provide administrative data within 30 days from the date the request is received. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  (6) If the head of a public institution determines to provide administrative data at a request for the provision of administrative data under paragraphs (3) and (4), he or she shall provide the Minister of Data and Statistics with such administrative data within 30 days from the date the request is received. <Added on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (7) Notwithstanding paragraph (5) or (6), where providing administrative data within 30 days is not possible due to unavoidable reasons, including cases in which the processing and handling of administrative data requested take considerable time, the head of a public institution may extend the period for provision within the scope of 10 days after consultation according to the following classifications: <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. In cases of a request under paragraph (1): Consultation with the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government;
  2. Where a request is made under paragraphs (3) and (4): Consultation with the Minister of Data and Statistics and the heads of designated statistics service agencies.

Article 39 (Grounds for exceptions to provision of administrative data) "Good cause prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 24 (4) of the Act means any of the following: <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Where the head of a public agency has reasonable reasons to believe that the vital national interest is likely to be significantly harmed if administrative data on national secret having grave influence on national security, national defense, reunification, diplomatic relations, etc. are provided for the production of statistics;
  2. Where the head of a public agency has reasonable reasons to believe that implementation of duties is substantially impracticable or a criminal defendant's right to fair trial is violated if administrative data related to a trial underway or to the prevention of a crime, investigation, institution and maintenance of prosecution, enforcement of a penalty, correction and preventive order are provided for the production of statistics;
  3. Where the head of a public agency has reasonable reasons to believe that vital confidential business information of an individual or enterprise is significantly harmed if administrative data related to the development of new products or research on new technologies of an individual or enterprise, or to manufacturing methods or sales methods being kept confidential by making considerable effort are provided for the production of statistics;
  4. Where the head of a public agency has reasonable reasons to believe that the protection of the life, body or property of an individual is significantly impeded if administrative data related to the political, religious or sexual orientation or livelihood of an individual are provided for the production of statistics.

Article 39-2 (Information security measures for administrative data) A person who is provided with administrative data pursuant to Article 24 (4) of the Act shall take preliminary technical and physical measures necessary to ensure the following security under Article 24 (6) of the Act:
  1. Measures to control access to administrative data and restrict access rights;
  2. Application of encryption technology that can safely store and transmit such data or measures corresponding thereto;
  3. Measures to keep records of access to administrative data and to prevent forgery or alteration;
  4. Installation and update of administrative data security programs;
  5. Physical measures, including the installation of administrative data storage facilities or locking devices.
  [This Article Added on Jan. 2, 2024]
  [(Previous) Article 39-2 moved to Article 39-3 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 39-3 (Scope of computerized data on family registration) The Minister of Data and Statistics may request the Minister of National Court Administration to provide data regarding family relations, nationality, marital status, types of divorce, and other related matters under Article 24-2 (1) of the Act. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jun. 27, 2017]
  [Moved from Article 39-2; (Previous) Article 39-3 moved to Article 39-4 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 39-4 (Scope of vital statistics survey) (1) To prepare the vital statistics under Article 24-2 (4) of the Act, the Minister of Data and Statistics shall conduct surveys on births, deaths, marriages, and divorces (hereinafter referred to as the "vital statistics survey"). <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) "Data prescribed by Presidential Decree, which are prepared and submitted by a person who files an application while he or she files an application for registration of a birth, death, marriage, divorce, etc. pursuant to other Acts" in Article 24-2 (4) 2 of the Act means the following data:
  1. An application for registration concerning birth, death, marriage, divorce, etc. prepared by a person who files an application pursuant to the Act on the Registration of Family Relations;
  2. Documents attached to an application under subparagraph 1.
  (3) The scope of a vital statistics survey shall include the following:
  1. Matters regarding persons who were born, dead, got married or got divorced;
  2. Matters regarding parents of children born;
  3. Matters regarding applicants for registration of births or deaths.
  (4) Items of a vital statistics survey shall be items prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree, such as names, resident registration numbers or alien registration numbers, and addresses. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) Matters concerning the submission, review, and management of data necessary for the vital statistics survey shall be prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jun. 27, 2017]
  [Moved from Article 39-3 <Jan. 2, 2024>]

Article 40 (Procedures and methods for requesting to submit data) (1) If the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government intends to request individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. to submit data pursuant to Article 25 (2) of the Act, he or she shall, in advance, give them a period of at least seven days; provided, this shall not apply if there is any compelling reason not to do so, including cases in which the date by which gathering of data for relevant designated statistics is to be completed is imminent. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018>
  (2) A request to submit data under paragraph (1) shall be made in writing (including a document in electronic form), and the following matters shall be clearly stated in writing: <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018>
  1. Name or title and address of a person who receives a request to submit data;
  2. Title of designated statistics and approval number or consultation number for the production of statistics;
  3. Details of data to be submitted;
  4. Deadline and method to submit data;
  5. Name of a central administrative agency or local government to which data are to be submitted, and department and person in charge;
  6. Guidance on disposition of an administrative fine under Article 41 of the Act where a person or organization fails to comply with a request to submit data.
  [Title Amended on February 20, 2018]

Article 41 (Requests to make requests to submit data and handling of requests) (1) If the head of a designated statistics service agency deems it necessary for producing the designated statistics under his or her jurisdiction, he or she may request the Minister of Data and Statistics to require the submission of data under Article 25 (3) of the Act. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) A request under paragraph (1) shall be made in writing (including a document in electronic form), and matters under the subparagraphs of Article 40 (2) shall be clearly stated in writing.
  (3) Upon receiving a request under paragraph (1), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall review the necessity and appropriateness of requiring the submission of data, and other related matters, determine whether to require the submission of data, and notify the head of the requesting designated statistics service agency of the decision, within 30 days from the date of receipt, unless there is a compelling reason not to do so. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [Title Amended on February 20, 2018]

Article 41-2 (Procedures and methods for conducting on-site investigations) Where the head of a statistics service agency requests the Minister of Data and Statistics, under the latter part of Article 26 (1) of the Act, to determine whether statistics may be produced through surveys or verifications using administrative data available for use by that agency, Article 24 (3) and (4) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the method of making such request and to the notification of the results. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Feb. 20, 2018]

SECTION 2 Dissemination and Use of Statistics

Article 42 (Method of announcement of statistics) (1) Publication under Article 27 (1) and (5) of the Act shall be given by affixing the national statistics approval (consultation) mark under Article 32 and providing press releases to media outlets, publishing statistics publications, or furnishing data through electronic media or information and communications networks, or by any other method that can broadly disseminate statistics. <Amended on Feb. 20, 2018; Sep. 30, 2025>
  (2) Matters to be announced along with statistics pursuant to Article 27 (2) of the Act shall be those related to the statistics, among the following matters:
  1. Outline of statistics, such as the title of statistics and purpose, subjects, time and period of production;
  2. Methods of producing statistics, such as sampling method and method of gathering, processing, correcting, supplementing and analyzing data;
  3. Matters regarding the quality of statistics, such as methods of substituting errors and non-response and rate of non-response;
  4. Matters for the convenience of users, such as explanation of principal terms or signs, schedule of announcement and contact information of persons in charge;
  5. Other matters necessary for the accurate use of statistics.

Article 42-2 (Request for advance provision) A person who intends to receive statistics prepared for performing the relevant duties prior to publication under Article 27-2 (2) 2 (b) of the Act shall submit to the head of the statistics service agency a document (including electronic documents) that contains the following matters; in such cases, if he or she intends to modify any matters submitted, he or she shall submit the modified matters to the head of the statistics service agency. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025>
  1. The statistics that he or she intends to be provided with;
  2. Necessity of provision and plans for utilization;
  3. The period for which the statistics will be provided; provided, the period shall not exceed 1 year;
  4. A person in charge to whom the statistics are to be provided.
  [This Article Added on Jul. 26, 2016]

Article 42-3 (Exceptions to advance provision of produced statistics, disclosure) (1) When a statistics service agency provides statistics produced under Article 27-2 (3) of the Act, it shall record and preserve the title of the statistics, the method of provision, and other matters in a management ledger prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" referred to in the proviso of Article 27-2 (4) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where needs arise for international cooperation, such as that statistics are submitted to an international organization at its request;
  2. Where relevant agencies are requested to take urgent measures due to economic crisis, market instability, etc.;
  3. Where relevant agencies are requested to take urgent measures due to epidemics, natural disasters, calamities, etc.;
  4. Where preparation of advance measures is necessary as economic crisis, market instability, etc. may have an influence on national defense, unification, foreign relations, etc.
  (3) The head of the statistics service agency shall prepare the results of the comparison and verification under Article 27-2 (5) of the Act as prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree and shall post them on the website of the agency. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jul. 26, 2016]

Article 43 (Establishment and operation of statistics database) (1) To enable statistics service agencies to share and utilize statistical data, the Minister of Data and Statistics shall prepare and distribute standard classification codes for the statistics database under Article 28 of the Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as the "statistics database"). <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) The Minister of Data and Statistics may provide statistics service agencies with technical support necessary for establishing and managing the statistics database. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) The Minister of Data and Statistics may determine matters necessary for the efficient operation of the statistics database. <Amended on Jun. 29, 2010; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) The Minister of Data and Statistics shall periodically review and update statistics data and explanatory notes on a statistics database. <Added on Jun. 29, 2010>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jul. 1, 2009]

Article 44 (Entrustment of duties of issuance and sale of statistics publications) (1) Under Article 29 (1) of the Act, the Minister of Data and Statistics may entrust the publication and sale of statistical publications to an institution, etc. that meets the requirements under Article 52 (1) and is designated by the Minister of Data and Statistics. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) When the Minister of Data and Statistics designates an entrusted institution under paragraph (1), they shall publicly notify in the Official Gazette the name of the entrusted institution, the details and procedures of the entrusted duties, and other necessary matters. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>

Article 45 (Scope of statistics publications to be submitted) "Statistics publications prescribed by Presidential Decree" referred to in the former part of Article 29 (2) of the Act means publications with the main purpose of recording the results of the production of statistics, such as statistics monthly, annals of statistics, yearbook of statistics and statistical survey reports, and statistical data (including analysis and explanation); provided, the policy white papers, duty manuals, reports on research results issued after processing and analyzing all kinds of statistical data with the main purpose of research or statistics publications for reference of duties within an agency that are not for public disclosure shall be excluded.

Article 45-2 (Keeping of statistics data and methods of management) (1) The heads of statistics service agencies shall keep and manage statistical data in an electronic database or other media under Article 29-2 (1) of the Act to prevent their loss.
  (2) The Minister of Data and Statistics may establish necessary standards, including operational guidelines for the retention and management of statistical data to ensure its accurate management, and may recommend such standards to statistics service agencies. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]

Article 45-3 (Provision of statistical register data) (1) The head of a statistics service agency intending to request the provision of statistical register data pursuant to Article 29-3 (1) of the Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as "requesting agency") shall make a written request (including a document in electronic form) containing the following matters:
  1. Name and address of the requesting agency;
  2. Title of statistical register data;
  3. Purpose of using statistical register data;
  4. Contents and scope of statistical register data;
  5. Methods of providing statistical register data;
  6. Methods of protecting statistical register data.
  (2) Upon receiving a request under paragraph (1), the Minister of Data and Statistics shall, within 30 days from the date of receipt, review the matters specified in paragraph (1) 3 through 6, determine whether to provide the data, and determine the scope or method of provision, and shall notify the head of the requesting agency of the decision; provided, if it is impracticable to determine and provide the data within 30 days due to unavoidable circumstances, the Minister of Data and Statistics may extend the provision period, within a limit of 10 days, in consultation with the head of the requesting agency. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) If the Minister of Data and Statistics provides statistical register data under paragraph (2), the Minister shall utilize the statistical data center under Article 31-2 (1) of the Act; provided, if the head of the requesting agency requests provision in another manner, including requesting provision stored on electronic media, the Minister of Data and Statistics may provide the data in another manner in consultation with the head of the requesting agency, taking into account the level of protection required for individuals, corporations, organizations, or other entities. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) If the Minister of Data and Statistics provides statistical register data under paragraph (2), the Minister may impose necessary expenses or fees on the requesting agency. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (5) If statistical register data are used for educational or research activities, or if necessary for the development of national statistics, the Minister of Data and Statistics may reduce the fee under paragraph (4); provided, if the requesting agency is a central administrative agency or a local government, the fee shall be exempted. <Added on Dec. 24, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jan. 2, 2024]

Article 46 (Requests for statistical data by statistics service agencies and provision) (1) The head of a statistics service agency intending to request the provision of statistical data pursuant to Article 30 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "requesting agency") shall make a written request (including a document in electronic form) containing the following matters:
  1. Name and address of the requesting agency;
  2. Title of statistical data;
  3. Purpose of using statistical data;
  4. Contents and scope of statistical data;
  5. Methods of providing statistical data;
  6. Methods of protecting statistical data.
  (2) The head of a statistics service agency in receipt of a request under paragraph (1) (hereinafter referred to as "providing agency") shall examine matters under paragraph (1) 3 through 6, determine whether to provide statistical data, scope, method of provision, etc., and notify the head of the requesting agency thereof within 30 days from the date he or she receives such request; provided, if it is impracticable to make determination and provide statistical data within 30 days due to unavoidable reasons, he or she shall consult with the head of the requesting agency and extend the period up to 10 days.
  (3) The methods of providing statistical data under paragraph (2) shall include recording on electronic media, using information and communications networks or providing copies or printouts, but the method designated by the head of the requesting agency shall be given priority: Provide, That where there is good cause, including cases in which it is deemed necessary to protect the information of individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. included in the statistical data or deemed that the method designated by the head of the requesting agency is inappropriate, the head of the providing agency may use other methods after consultation with the head of the requesting agency.
  (4) If the head of the providing agency provides statistical data under paragraph (2), they may impose the necessary expenses or fees on the requesting agency. <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025>
  (5) The head of the providing agency may reduce or exempt fees under paragraph (4) if statistical data are used for educational and research activities or necessary for the development, etc. of national statistics; provided, if the requesting agency is a central administrative agency or local government, such fees shall be exempted. <Added on Dec. 24, 2024>

Article 47 (Application for statistical register data or statistical data by users of statistics and provision thereof) (1) A person who intends to use statistical register data or statistical data under Article 31 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "user of statistics") shall make a written application (including a document in electronic format) specifying the following matters: <Amended on Jul. 26, 2016; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Name (name of an institution, etc. in cases of an institution, etc.) and address of the user of statistics;
  2.The name of the statistical register data or statistical data;
  3.The purpose of using the statistical register data or statistical data;
  4. The contents and scope of the statistical register data or statistical data;
  5. The methods of providing the statistical register data or statistical data;
  6. The methods of protecting the statistical register data or statistical data;
  (2) The head of a statistics service agency (referring to the Minister of Data and Statistics in the case of statistical register data; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article) shall determine whether to provide statistical data and other matters according to the results of examination under Article 31 (3) of the Act and notify the user of statistics thereof within 30 days from the date of receipt of an application under paragraph (1); provided, where providing statistical register data or statistical data within 30 days is impracticable due to unavoidable reasons, such as processing, handling, etc. of statistical register data or statistical data, he or she may consult with the user of statistics and extend the period by up to 10 days. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Dec. 24, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  (3) "Information prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as names of businesses, business categories, domiciles, etc." referred to in Article 31 (3) 2 of the Act means the names, categories, domiciles, and telephone numbers of businesses. <Added on Jul. 26, 2016; Sep. 12, 2023; Jan. 2, 2024>
  (4) Article 45-3 (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the methods of providing the users of statistics with statistical register data. In such cases, "the head of a requesting agency" shall be construed as "user of statistics". <Added on Jan. 2, 2024>
  (5) Article 46 (3) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the methods of providing the users of statistics with statistical data. In such cases, "the head of a requesting agency" shall be construed as "user of statistics," and "providing institution" as "statistics service agency." <Amended on Jul. 26, 2016; Jan. 2, 2024>
  (6) In principle, expenses or fees necessary for the provision of statistical register data or statistical data under paragraph (2) shall be borne by users of the statistical data. <Amended on Jul. 26, 2016; Jan. 2, 2024>
  (7) The head of a statistics service agency may reduce or exempt fees under paragraph (6) if statistical register data or statistical data are used for educational and research activities or necessary for the development of national statistics; provided, if users of statistics are State agencies or local governments, fees shall be exempted. <Added on Dec. 24, 2024>
  [Title Amended on Jan. 2, 2024]

Article 48 (Protection of statistical register data or statistical data) (1) If the head of a statistics service agency (in cases of the statistics register data, referring to the Commissioner of the Statistics Korea; hereafter in this Article the same shall apply) provides the statistics register data or statistical data under Article 29-3 (3) and (4), 30 (2), or 31 (3) of the Act, he or she may impose restrictions on the purpose, methods, etc. of using the statistics register data or statistical data and other necessary matters for the head of a requesting agency or user of statistics so as to protect information, etc. of individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the head of a statistics service agency provides statistical register data or statistical data pursuant to Article 29-3 (3) or (4), 30 (2), or 31 (3) of the Act, he or she may request the head of a requesting agency or user of statistics to take measures necessary for the following matters in order to ensure the security of the statistical register data or statistical data, etc.:
  1. Matters regarding the prohibition of duplication or lending of provided statistical register data or statistical data;
  2.Matters regarding measures to ensure the security of data, such as the destruction of the provided statistical register data or statistical data after use;
  (3) Where the head of a requesting agency or a user of statistics falls under any of the following cases, the head of a statistics service agency may suspend the provision of the statistical register data or statistical data or restrict the scope of provision of the statistical register data or statistical data:
  1. Where he or she fails to comply with the restrictions under paragraph (1);
  2. Where he or she fails to take measures under paragraph (2);
  3. Where the head of a statistics service agency deems that the measures taken under paragraph (2) are insufficient.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Jan. 2, 2024]

Article 49 (Establishment and operation of deliberative council on provision of statistical data) (1) To deliberate on the following matters, the head of a statistics service agency may have a deliberative council on the provision of statistical data (hereinafter referred to as "council") under his or her control: <Amended on Jul. 26, 2016; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Provision of statistics under Article 14-2 (1) of the Act;
  2. Production of new statistics under Article 21-2 (2) of the Act;
  2-2. Determination of whether to provide statistical register data, the scope of provision thereof, etc. under Article 29-3 (2) of the Act;
  3. Provision of statistical data under Article 30 (1) of the Act;
  4. Use of statistics register data or statistical data under Article 31 (3) of the Act.
  (2) The composition and operation of a council and other necessary matters shall be determined by the head of the relevant statistics service agency.

Article 49-2 (Establishment and operation of statistics data center) (1) The statistical data center under Article 31-2 (1) of the Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as the "data center") shall perform the following duties: <Amended on Sep. 30, 2025>
  1. Acquisition and management of statistical register data, statistical data, administrative data, and data from the private sector;
  1-2. Support for de-identification of data, linkage across datasets, and data utilization;
  2. Periodic inspection and security management of equipment and systems;
  3. Approval and management of applications for use by users;
  4. Approval for bringing-in and taking-out of equipment and management thereof;
  5. Other support for research and analysis related to the utilization of data under subparagraph 1.
  (2) A data center shall be equipped with security facilities to control access.
  (3) To ensure the security of the data center, the Minister of Data and Statistics shall take necessary technical, administrative, and physical measures. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (4) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (3), matters necessary for establishing and operating the data center shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Data and Statistics. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Jan. 2, 2024]

Article 50 (Measures for protection of confidentiality) (1) The head of a statistics service agency shall take measures necessary for the management of survey questionnaires, report forms, electronic media on which matters constituting confidential information of individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. gathered in the course of the production of statistics are recorded, and other relevant data so that such matters are protected pursuant to Article 33 of the Act.
  (2) If the Minister of Data and Statistics delegates or entrusts the provision of statistical register data or statistical data under Article 37 (2) of the Act, he or she shall determine restrictions or procedures necessary for the following matters and require the agency to which the provision of statistical register data or statistical data is delegated or entrusted to comply with such restrictions or procedures: Added on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Matters regarding the prohibition or restriction of re-delegation or re-entrustment;
  2. Matters regarding the duplication of the statistical register data or statistical data;
  3. Matters regarding the management and sale of the statistical register data or statistical data;
  4. Other matters necessary for the protection of confidential information of individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. under the Act or this Decree.
  (3) Where the head of a statistics service agency delegates or entrusts other statistics service agencies or relevant institutions with the processing or provision of statistical data, he or she shall determine restrictions or procedures necessary for the following matters and have agencies and institutions delegated or entrusted with the processing of statistical data follow them: <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Matters regarding the prohibition or restriction of re-delegation or re-entrustment;
  2. Matters regarding the duplication of statistical data files;
  3. Matters regarding the management and sale of statistical data;
  4. Other matters necessary for the protection of confidential information of individuals, corporations, organizations, etc. under the Act or this Decree.
  (4) In cases falling under paragraphs (2) and (3), the Minister of Data and Statistics or the head of a statistics service agency shall occasionally inspect the current status of the processing of statistical register data or statistical data, the records and actual conditions related to the management, etc. of statistical register data or statistical data and details of input and output of data, with respect to an institution delegated or entrusted with the processing or provision of statistical register data or statistical data. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>

CHAPTER V SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 51 (Delegation and entrustment of authority of heads of central administrative agencies) (1) Where it is deemed necessary to facilitate the production of all kinds of statistics, such as censuses under Article 2-4 conducted nationwide pursuant to Article 37 (1) of the Act, the head of a central administrative agency may delegate the following authority to the heads of affiliated institutions or Mayors/Do Governors, or entrust to the heads of other administrative agencies or designated statistics service agencies, as prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decrees or Ministerial Decrees: <Amended on Mar. 18, 2013; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Design (including design of enumeration districts, survey questionnaires and samples) and development of surveys for the production of statistics;
  2. Recruitment, employment, education and training, and management of statistical researchers (including statistical survey advisors and examiners of the contents of statistical surveys), and issuance of certificates;
  3. Distribution, receipt, collection and submission of statistical survey questionnaires;
  4. Examination, ascertainment and supplementation of the contents of statistical survey questionnaires;
  5. Input, processing and submission of statistical survey data;
  6. Guidance, supervision and publicity of the duties of statistical surveys;
  7. Analysis of gathered data or other matters necessary for the production of statistics.
  (2) Where it is deemed necessary for the convenience of users of statistical data pursuant to Article 37 (1) of the Act, the heads of central administrative agencies may delegate his or her authority concerning the dissemination of statistics under Article 28 (1) of the Act to the heads of affiliated institutions or entrust the heads of other administrative agencies or designated statistics service agencies therewith.

Article 52 (Entrustment of duties of the Minister of Data and Statistics) (1) Pursuant to Article 37 (2) of the Act, the Minister of Data and Statistics may entrust agencies, etc. designated by him or her, among agencies meeting all the following requirements, with the duties falling under subparagraphs 1, 1-2, 3, 5, and 6 of that paragraph: <Amended on Mar. 18, 2013; Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. It shall be a juristic person incorporated according to the Civil Act or other Acts;
  2. It shall carry on business of development and promotion of statistics or diagnosis of the quality of statistics;
  3. It shall have an organization and human resources necessary for the performance of entrusted duties;
  4. It shall have public credibility and expertise necessary for the performance of entrusted duties.
  (2) When the Minister of Data and Statistics designates an entrusted institution under paragraph (1), they shall publicly notify in the Official Gazette the name of the entrusted institution, the details and procedures of the entrusted duties, and other necessary matters. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  [Title Amended on Oct. 1, 2025]

Article 52-2 (Entrustment of duties by heads of statistics service agencies) (1) Where the head of a statistics service agency entrusts the business affairs under Article 37 (3) of the Act to the Minister of Data and Statistics, they shall submit to the Minister of Data and Statistics the data necessary for processing the entrusted business affairs. <Amended on Oct. 1, 2025>
  (2) Where the head of a statistics service agency intends to entrust the business affairs under the subparagraphs of Article 37 (3) of the Act to the Minister of Data and Statistics, they shall have a prior consultation with the Minister of Data and Statistics on the matters necessary for processing the entrusted business affairs, including the subject, scope, method, and timing of the retention, management, and provision of statistical data. <Amended on Jul. 26, 2016; Oct. 1, 2025>
  [This Article Added on Mar. 18, 2013]

Article 52-3 (Processing of sensitive information and personally identifiable information) (1) The head of a statistics service agency may manage data containing sensitive information under Article 23 of the Personal Information Protection Act (hereinafter referred to as "sensitive information") or data containing resident registration numbers, passport numbers, driver's license numbers, or alien registration numbers under Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act (hereinafter referred to as "resident registration numbers, etc."), if it is inevitable to perform the following business affairs: <Amended on Sep. 12, 2023; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Business affairs regarding the production of statistics approved by the Minister of Data and Statistics under Article 18 (1) of the Act;
  2. Business affairs regarding the production of statistics in consultation with the Minister of Data and Statistics under Article 20 (1) of the Act.
  3. Business affairs regarding provision of statistical data under Article 30 (1) of the Act;
  4. Business affairs regarding the use of statistical register data or statistical data under Article 31 (3) of the Act (limited to sensitive information).
  (2) The head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government may manage data containing sensitive information or resident registration numbers, etc., if it is inevitable to conduct business affairs regarding requests for the provision of administrative data under Article 24 of the Act. <Amended on Sep. 12, 2023>
  (3) The Minister of Data and Statistics may process data containing sensitive information or resident registration numbers, if it is unavoidable for the performance of the following business affairs: <Amended on Sep. 12, 2023; Jan. 2, 2024; Oct. 1, 2025>
  1. Business affairs regarding the establishment and operation of the statistical registers under Article 5-3 (1) of the Act;
  2. Business affairs regarding the census under Article 5-4 (1) of the Act;
  3. Business affairs regarding requests to provide data under Article 24-2 (1) and (2) of the Act;
  4. Business affairs regarding the provision of statistical register data under Article 29-3 (1) of the Act.
  [This Article Added on Jun. 27, 2017]
  [Title Amended on Sep. 12, 2023]

CHAPTER VI PENALTY PROVISIONS

Article 53 (Standards for imposition of administrative fines) The standards for imposition of administrative fines under Article 41 (1) through (4) of the Act are as listed in the Appendix. <Amended on Jul. 26, 2016>
